.IX Title "BPSENDTEST 1"
.TH BPSENDTEST 1 2025-11-26 "perl v5.38.2" "BP executables"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH NAME
bpsendtest \- Bundle Protocol (BP) file\-based throughput testing utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
\&\fBbpsendtest\fR [\-rep \fIrepetitions\fR] [\-ttl \fIttl\fR] [\-qos \fIqos\fR] [\-nofile] \fIsrcEid\fR \fIdestEid\fR \fIfile\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
\&\fBNOTE: THIS UTILITY IS FOR TESTING PURPOSES ONLY\fR
.PP
\&\fBbpsendtest\fR is a modified variant of \fBbpsendfile\fR and is intended 
to serve as the counterpart to \fBbprecvtest\fR. 
It first generates a minimal bundle with the contents "Go" to serve 
as a pilot bundle and inform \fBbprecvtest\fR to begin its timer.
If \-nofile is not specified, it then creates a bundle from the supplied 
file identified by \fIfile\fR and sends that bundle a number of times 
equal to \fIrepetitions\fR to the endpoint specified by \fIdestEid\fR. 
If \-nofile is specified, \fIfile\fR is interpreted to be an integer describing the number 
of bytes to generate and send as a bundle.
The bundle is sent once if \fIrepetitions\fR is not supplied.
.PP
The bundle is sent with no custody transfer
requested.  When \fIqos\fR is omitted, the bundle is sent at
standard priority; for details of the \fIqos\fR parameter,
see \fBbptrace\fR\|(1) or run \f(CW\*(C`bpsendtest \-h\*(C'\fR.  \fIttl\fR, if not specified, defaults to 300
seconds (5 minutes).  \fBNOTE\fR that the final three arguments \fBMUST\fR
be \fIsrcEid\fR \fIdestEid\fR \fIfile\fR in their respective order.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.IX Header "EXIT STATUS"
.IP """0""" 4
.IX Item """0"""
\&\fBbpsendtest\fR has terminated.
.SH FILES
.IX Header "FILES"
No configuration files are needed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.IX Header "ENVIRONMENT"
No environment variables apply.
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
.IX Header "DIAGNOSTICS"
The following diagnostics may be issued to the \fBion.log\fR log file:
.IP "Can't attach to BP." 4
.IX Item "Can't attach to BP."
\&\fBbpadmin\fR has not yet initialized BP operations.
.IP "Can't open own endpoint." 4
.IX Item "Can't open own endpoint."
Another BP application task currently has \fIsrcEid\fR open for
bundle origination and reception.  Try again after that task has terminated.
If no such task exists, it may have crashed while still holding the endpoint
open; the easiest workaround is to select a different source endpoint.
.IP "Can't stat the file" 4
.IX Item "Can't stat the file"
Operating system error.  Check errtext, correct problem, and rerun.
.IP "bpsendtest can't create file ref." 4
.IX Item "bpsendtest can't create file ref."
Probably an unrecoverable database error, in which case the local ION
node must be terminated and re-initialized.
.IP "bpsendtest can't create ZCO." 4
.IX Item "bpsendtest can't create ZCO."
Probably an unrecoverable database error, in which case the local ION
node must be terminated and re-initialized.
.IP "bpsendtest can't send file in bundle." 4
.IX Item "bpsendtest can't send file in bundle."
BP system error.  Check for earlier diagnostic messages describing the
cause of the error; correct problem and rerun.
.SH BUGS
.IX Header "BUGS"
Report bugs to <https://github.com/nasa\-jpl/ION\-DTN/issues>
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
